Rule 1 (batch tensors must be 3-D and mutually compatible for bmm)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 3 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 3 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) ∧ shape(v_1, 2) = shape(v_2, 1)
>>
Rule 2 (input must be broadcastable to (n, p) and have at most 2 dims)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 0) ∨ (ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_3, 2)) ∨ (ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ (shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 1)) ∧ (shape(v_1, 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_3, 2)))
>>
Rule 3 (out, if provided, must be a 2-D tensor with shape (n, p))
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_3) = 2 ∧ shape(v_3, 0) = shape(v_1, 1) ∧ shape(v_3, 1) = shape(v_2, 2)
>>
Rule 4 (batch1 and batch2 dtypes must match for matmul)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 5 (out dtype must match computation dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1)
